  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   The current heuristic approach may get stuck in local optima. We need a more systematic method: divide the interval [0,2] into four equal parts and ensure that the function has minimal overlap at shifts corresponding to multiples of 1/4. This approach leverages symmetry and periodic alignment, which should reduce the maximum overlap compared to the parent's method.\n\n   Key changes:\n   - Use 8 points for symmetry and periodicity\n   - Ensure periodic consistency with interval alignment\n   - Gradually refine resolution from coarse to fine\n\n   This addresses the bottleneck of getting stuck in local optima by focusing on symmetry and periodic behavior, which are known to reduce discrepancy.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - Representation: h(x) over [0,2] with periodic extensions implied at half-integers for alignment\n   - Variables: Function values at 8 key points ensuring integral equals 1\n   - Objective: Minimize maximum overlap integral, defined as:\n     max_k \u222b h(x) * (1 - h(x+k)) dx\n   with overlapping definitions accounting for domain boundaries\n   - Constraints:\n     0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n     \u03a3h[i] = initial_n/2 (500 in parent case)\n   - Optimization: Feature alignment phase followed by gradient-based polishing\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   a. Phase Zero: Coarse resolution (8 points)\n      - Generate candidates with periodic symmetry:\n        h[0] = h[4], h[1] = h[5], h[2] = h[6], h[3] = h[7]\n      - Enforce integral = 4 (since 8 points, integral = n/2)\n      - Initialize with periodic \"comb\" pattern\n      - Compute objective\n\n   b. Phase One: Medium resolution (16 points, then 32)\n      - Upfloyd-based adjustment: maintain periodicity with 8-point pattern\n      - Use smooth_max_val() and smooth_max_grad_full() for gradient\n      - Add epsilon to maintain bounds\n      - Check constraints after each refinement\n\n   c. Phase Two: Fine resolution (64, 128)\n      - Similar periodic enforcement but using quadratic constraints\n      - Time budget allocation: 40% Phase Zero, 30% Two, 30% Three\n      - Move to next phase when current max overlap doesn't decrease or time expires\n\n   d. Phase Three: Final optimization\n      - Full 500-point spectrum\n      - Start from best of previous phases\n      - Minimize using L-BFGS-B with n/2 equality constraint\n      - Final projection to bounds and integral\n\n   e. Objective computation:\n      dx = 2/n_points\n      correlation = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n      c5 = (correlation * dx).max()\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations:\n   Default parameters:\n      - Base: n_start = 8, then 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 1000\n      - Early termination based on objective improvement\n      - Multiplicative learning rate: 0.998 for gradient descent\n      - Golden ratio sampling for secondary initialization attempts\n\n   Informational variations (smarter but more complex):\n      - Fourier-transform inspired low-pass filtering (use for local optimization)\n      - Convolution-based correlation minimization at periodic patterns\n      - Bayesian optimization for choosing optimal phase transitions\n\n   Phase time = 280 seconds (majority allocated to fine refinement)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n   Time estimation:\n      - Phase Z: 280 sec\n      - n-transitions: 350 ms per doubling\n      Each phase: Most expensive is fine phase with L-BFGS-B rules\n      Test check: 500 points, one constraint - ~2-3 minutes\n      Total subject to time limits but should complete within budget\n\n   Finite values: Force bounds and apply clip on NaNs\n   Dimension consistency: Use helper that maps phases\n   Solver response: Use n/2 sum constraint for n=500\n   Robustness: Always fall back to parent's solution if stuck\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n   Feasibility checks:\n      - h bound check: 0 <= h[i] <= 1 for all i\n      - Integral check: abs(sum(h)-n/2)<1e-6\n      - C5 object: (np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full')*dx).max()\n   Return contract:\n      - h_values: Array passes above checks\n      - c5_bound: Expressed as float\n      - n_points: Original 500 unless budget exceeded\n   Validation at end: Re-evaluate using exact objective\n   }}",
